From 06ddafb247b892bdfcfc621c4a5308ce6edc71ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Life OS Dev <lifeos@local>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 19:39:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(test): remove duplicate test annotation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

GitHub Actions run 36129867061, :app:compileDebugUnitTestKotlin reported:

  RestoreCoordinatorTest.kt:782:5 This annotation is not repeatable

`closetRevert_coversTheSwapOnwardsButNeverCommitsOrPreparing` carried two
@Test annotations (lines 765 and 782) with a KDoc block wedged between them.
JUnit's @Test is not repeatable, so the second one is a hard error.

The two KDoc blocks described the same predicate from two angles and overlapped
substantially: the first introduced swapInScope and the half-restore it guards,
the second enumerated the state table and why COMMITTED, FAILED and ROLLED_BACK
are cleanup-only. The second is the superset, so the first is dropped and its
one point of substance — that COMMITTED deliberately does not un-swap, which is
where a "false" answer costs the user half their data — is already stated in the
surviving block. One @Test and one KDoc remain.

No assertion, no test body and no test-local helper changed. RestoreCoordinator
production code and the restore state machine are untouched.

Whole-tree audit: a state-machine scanner over all 24 test files pairs every
annotation run with its declaration and reports repeated names across
@Test/@Before/@After/@RunWith/@Rule/@Ignore. Run against the pre-fix revision it
reproduces exactly this error at lines 765 and 782; on the fixed tree it reports
0 duplicates. Two flagged duplicate `fun` names were checked by hand and are
local helpers nested inside different test bodies, not clashing methods.
---
 .../com/qq/closie/data/backup/RestoreCoordinatorTest.kt  | 9 ---------
 1 file changed, 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/src/test/java/com/qq/closie/data/backup/RestoreCoordinatorTest.kt b/app/src/test/java/com/qq/closie/data/backup/RestoreCoordinatorTest.kt
index 923a831..e49bc96 100644
--- a/app/src/test/java/com/qq/closie/data/backup/RestoreCoordinatorTest.kt
+++ b/app/src/test/java/com/qq/closie/data/backup/RestoreCoordinatorTest.kt
@@ -754,15 +754,6 @@ class RestoreCoordinatorTest {
         )
     }
 
-    /**
-     * The predicate's companion, and the one the recovery path actually reads when deciding whether
-     * the Closet may be the backup's version.
-     *
-     * A committed database does not un-swap the directory, so every database state needs the revert
-     * too. Getting this wrong in the "false" direction leaves the user with the backup's wardrobe and
-     * their own life-graph — the half-restore seen from the other side.
-     */
-    @Test
     /**
      * The Closet-revert half, held to its exact set of states.
      *
-- 
